.TH LQTH 1 "February 2026" "lqth 0.2.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lqth \- simple screenshot utility for X11

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lqth
.RI [ options ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lqth
is a simple screenshot utility for X11.
It captures screenshots and writes the image data in
.B farbfeld
format to standard output.

The output can be redirected to a file or piped into other tools
for conversion or further processing.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -d ", " --display " <X server address>"
Specify the X11 display to capture from.

.TP
.BR -w ", " --window " <window id>"
Capture a specific window by its X11 window ID.

.TP
.BR -s ", " --screen " <screen number>"
Capture a specific screen.
This option is only effective if no window is selected.

.TP
.BR -r ", " --region " <coordinates>"
Capture a rectangular region.
Coordinates must be specified in the following format:
.br
.BR x :<n>, y :<n>, w :<n>, h :<n>

.TP
.BR -v ", " --version
Show version information and exit.

.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show help and exit.

.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B libX11

.SH OPTIONAL DEPENDENCIES
To convert farbfeld output into common image formats, you can use:
.TP
.B ff2png
.TP
.B ff2jpg
.br
Available from:
.br
https://git.suckless.org/farbfeld/

.SH EXAMPLES
Take a screenshot of the full screen:
.RS
.B lqth > screen.ff
.RE

Capture the active window and convert to PNG:
.RS
.B lqth -w $(xdotool getactivewindow) | ff2png > window.png
.RE

Capture a specific region:
.RS
.B lqth -r $(xrectsel 'x:%x,y:%y,w:%w,h:%h') | ff2png > region.png
.RE

Capture a region and copy it to the clipboard:
.RS
.B lqth -r $(xrectsel 'x:%x,y:%y,w:%w,h:%h') | ff2png | xclip -sel clip -t image/png -i
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error.

